{"title":"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Terri produces a sequence of positive integers by following three rules.  She starts with a positive integer, then applies the appropriate rule to the result, and continues in this fashion.  \n</p><p>Rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: If the integer is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: If the integer is even and greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, divide it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: If the integer is odd and greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from it.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>A sample sequence: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b7530d092a8aae51e49fcc009d4e32e3690a06dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23, 18, 9, 81, 76, \\ldots .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cc3bd96fdcb8eec5c322794ba26025b3cd9112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98^\\text{th}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> term of the sequence that begins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da9781ffa2fcc41e0da643616d102d1d99b344c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98, 49, \\ldots .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901c9be8e08a83342559bf181d6b40a8676ef9b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 22 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 27 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"367\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each term after the first depends solely on the previous term, the sequence will repeat the same subsequence endlessly once a term appears twice.\n</p><p>The first terms of the sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150f668e59f83a72c5f1f4578151055546b50169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98, 49, 44, 22, 11, 6, 54, 27, 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"17\" />, and thus the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-term subsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370054d5cf83418cf34f5048d0b41a8a8b53b58b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22, 11, 6, 54, 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" /> repeats endlessly starting at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543fb688603e3a8d804b5ed862002dba8edc0425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> term.  \nSince the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543fb688603e3a8d804b5ed862002dba8edc0425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/928578bc80748103470694da6a14bf5d3c3c5b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$94^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> term is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and thus the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a8859e8405112e324745c9d52b389cf7439af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f934e81db5d9d890c83a5eed84cdf441096c6204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME\" title=\"1998 AJHSME\">1998 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 AJ